    "english":  "The hill-stream cascades down the face of the mountain,\nleaping over stone shelves like an unbridled horse of white foam.\nThe sweet honey drips from the combs nestled high on the rocks,\nout of reach of the forest bears that climb the crags at twilight.\nO lord of this wild mountain realm, your words are as sweet as that honey,\nyet your absence leaves a bitter wound in my companion\u0027s heart.\nHer slender form grows fragile as a wind-blown reed;\ndo not leave her to wither under the gaze of her watchful kin,\nbut bring the marriage procession to our gates without delay!",
